    "narrative": "**Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** headlines our slate as the undisputed strongest play of the day with an elite 85.99 score. Facing Whisenhunt, who struggles significantly with a 5.60 xERA, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and the protection of batting second, making him our primary engine for runs and RBI. **Daulton Varsho** is our secondary anchor at 68.65, taking full advantage of a plus-matchup against Klassen; his 10% dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed arm positions him as a high-upside play despite the suboptimal park factors. **Bryce Harper** remains a mandatory start at 66.65, utilizing a favorable park and strong underlying xwOBA to mitigate the threat posed by Gibson, C.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles regarding our depth. The most difficult bench decision was **Gleyber Torres**, who narrowly missed our 40-point \"Zebras\" floor with a 38.15 rating. While his leadoff position provides a +10% boost, the combination of an elite matchup against Ashcraft and a significant negative platoon effect forced him to the bench in favor of higher-efficiency starters like **Masyn Winn**. We are also wary of the heavy left-handed exposure in today's lineup; **Lawrence Butler** and **Justin Crawford** are battling significant negative platoon splits against Lynch IV and Gibson, C respectively, dropping their daily value into the marginal tier. \n\nOwners should monitor **Cal Raleigh** closely; while his 47.21 score is serviceable, he faces a tough assignment against Harrison. His value is tethered to his power potential, but the 19% reduction due to the SP\u2019s skill level creates a low floor for his batting average contribution today. **Braden Montgomery** is currently our \"wild card\" play; while his base projection is modest, the favorable wind-out conditions at the park provide a +5% boost that keeps him in the lineup over bench options like **Brendan Donovan**. We are keeping a close watch on **Tyler Freeman** and **Matt Chapman**, who remain inactive on the IL; ensure their roster spots are not hindering your ability to rotate in high-speed depth, as our strategy remains heavily anchored in preserving stolen base upside.",
